  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Meglumine antimonate is an antiprotozoal medicine used to treat leishmaniasis. It is listed as an essential medicine by the WHO, but in some databases it is classified as investigational rather than an approved drug.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2757969&quot;>Wikidata Q2757969</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>meglumine antimonate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>P01CB01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13732&quot;>DB13732</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/64953&quot;>64953</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2757969&quot;>Q2757969</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C7H18NO8Sb</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>365.98 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
